`WallpaperManager::sort()` sorted a `Vec` of wallpaper references then rebuilt a `HashMap` — but `HashMap` provides no insertion-order guarantees, so the sorted order was immediately discarded on every call.

## Changes

- **`indexmap` dependency** — added to workspace and `lwg-core`
- **`wallpapers` field** — changed from `HashMap<String, Wallpaper>` to `IndexMap<String, Wallpaper>`, which guarantees iteration in insertion order
- **`sort()` rewrite** — replaced the collect-sort-rebuild pattern with an in-place `IndexMap::sort_by` call; eliminates the intermediate `Vec` and the unnecessary per-entry clone

  ```rust
  // Before: sort Vec<&Wallpaper>, then rebuild a HashMap (order not preserved)
  let mut wallpapers: Vec<_> = self.wallpapers.values().collect();
  wallpapers.sort_by(|a, b| a.title.cmp(&b.title));
  self.wallpapers = wallpapers.into_iter().map(|w| (w.id.clone(), w.clone())).collect();

  // After: sort in-place on the IndexMap directly
  self.wallpapers.sort_by(|_, a, _, b| a.title.cmp(&b.title));
  ```

- **`delete()`** — replaced the now-deprecated `IndexMap::remove` with `shift_remove` to maintain entry order after deletion
- **`scan()` return type** — updated signature from `&HashMap<…>` to `&IndexMap<…>`

