`getAuth(app)` throws `FirebaseError: (auth/invalid-api-key)` at module load time when `VITE_FIREBASE_*` env vars are unset, killing the entire React render tree before mount.

### Firebase initialization (`firebaseConfig.js`)
- Validate `apiKey`/`projectId` exist before calling `initializeApp`
- Wrap init in try/catch; export `null` for `db`/`auth` when config is missing

```js
const isConfigValid = firebaseConfig.apiKey && firebaseConfig.projectId;
if (isConfigValid) {
  try {
    app = initializeApp(firebaseConfig);
    db = getFirestore(app);
    auth = getAuth(app);
  } catch (err) {
    console.error('Firebase initialization failed:', err);
  }
}
```

### Graceful degradation throughout the app
- **`SiteContentContext`**: Skip Firestore `onSnapshot` subscription when `db` is null; serve default content; guard all write ops (`saveContent`, `resetSection`, `resetAll`, `importJSON`)
- **`LoginGate` / `AdminContext`**: Guard `onAuthStateChanged`, `signInWithEmailAndPassword`, `signOut` against null `auth`

### Data collection (`JoinCTA`)
- Connected "Join Now" form to Firestore `subscribers` collection via `addDoc`
- Added Firestore security rules with field validation for the new collection

### Repo hygiene
- Added `dist/` to `.gitignore`; removed stale committed `dist/` and `node_modules/@vercel/analytics` from tracking

